 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Karaoke Sign-Up Sheet FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a karaoke sign up sheet?\", \"a\": \"A karaoke sign up sheet is the list a host runs the night from. Each line holds a singer's name and song, and the order of the lines decides who goes next. It can be a clipboard by the stage or a phone form that feeds a queue.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a karaoke sign up sheet?\", \"a\": \"Describe the night in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>: the fields, the rotation rule, and what happens when a song is taken or the set fills. Emergent builds the form and its database. Share the link, run a test round, then open it to singers.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many singers can a karaoke sign up sheet hold in an hour?\", \"a\": \"About 12, if you allow 5 minutes a turn. Those 5 minutes cover the song plus the handover between singers. If your crowd leans toward long ballads, budget 6 minutes a turn and open 10 slots an hour instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I reuse the same karaoke sign up sheet every week?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Keep one link and clear the queue at closing, and the sheet starts empty the next week. Emergent keeps past nights in a database you own, where you can see which singers come back. For a group that also tracks members and meeting duties, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/club-sign-up-sheet'>club sign up sheet</a> fits better.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a karaoke sign up sheet stop one person hogging the mic?\", \"a\": \"It limits each person to one song in each round. A repeat sign-up waits until the round ends. Post the limit on the screen before the first song, and the host never has to turn anyone down in person.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can singers fill in a karaoke sign up sheet on their phones?\", \"a\": \"Yes. They open the sign-up link, either typed in or scanned from a code on the table, and enter a name and a song on a short form. Keep it under four questions. Each entry joins the queue as soon as it is saved, and the host stops collecting paper slips.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a karaoke sign up sheet also collect food for a party?\", \"a\": \"Yes, though it reads better as its own section, so a song pick never waits on a dish choice. For a party where guests bring food, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/potluck-sign-up-sheet'>potluck sign up sheet</a> tracks who brings what by course. Emergent builds either one from a plain-English prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How should a karaoke sign up sheet work for a contest?\", \"a\": \"It should hold each singer's scores next to the song. Use the same judges and the same scale for every singer, such as 1 to 10, and agree on what earns a 10 before the first song. Decide in advance how a tie is broken, such as a short sing-off.\"}, {\"q\": \"What happens when a karaoke sign up sheet is full?\", \"a\": \"Later sign-ups go on a numbered waitlist, and the host calls them in order if a singer leaves or the set runs long. Tell each waitlisted singer their number. With Emergent, no cap limits sign-ups; the only limit is the slot count you choose.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a karaoke sign up sheet the same as a sign in sheet?\", \"a\": \"No. A sign up sheet books a turn that has not happened yet, while a sign in sheet records who has already arrived. If you need a record of everyone on a work site and when they came in, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/safety-sign-in-sheet'>safety sign in sheet</a> does that job.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
